  "final_answer_preview": "Criminal force is defined as the actual application of force against another person, whereas assault is characterized by gestures or preparations that lead a person to believe that force is imminent. Specifically, Section 130 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita states that an assault occurs when someone makes a gesture or preparation that causes another person to apprehend that they are about to face criminal force. In contrast, criminal force can be seen in actions that directly inflict harm or threaten harm, as illustrated in Section 129, where inciting a dog to attack someone constitutes the use of criminal force.",
